 "final": "-- Picks an element of a non-empty list by index seed % len.\n-- Floor modulo keeps the index in range for any seed, including negatives.\n-- Uses no capabilities, so the same seed always gives the same element.\n\npick(xs: List[int], seed: int) -> int =\n  pre xs.len() >= 1\n  post out == xs[seed % xs.len()]\n  ex pick([10, 20, 30], 4) == 20\n  ex pick([7], -5) == 7\n  ex pick([1, 2], 6) == pick([1, 2], 0)\n  xs[seed % xs.len()]\n",
